cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Heptagon Intersection Project: a Lean-verified bound of 38 for simple heptagons sharing no vertex, toward f(7,7)"
message: >-
  If you cite this repository, cite the release tag and commit you examined.
  What is kernel-checked in Lean 4: two simple heptagons whose boundaries meet
  in finitely many points and which share no vertex meet in at most 38 points,
  and 38 is attained. f(7,7) = 38 is NOT established here. It additionally
  depends on the vertex-coincidence reduction of Ackerman-Keszegh-Rote (2022),
  Sect. 9.1. That reduction is not formalized, and its applicability to these
  definitions is unresolved. No independent review has been completed. The
  problem has been submitted to TheoremDB for review (pending). See README.md,
  "Current status".
